# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored). Prod values are Wrangler secrets.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string
# Signs unsubscribe links (task 126) — its own secret, not the auth one.
# Required: without it no optional email goes and every link is refused.
UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET=generate-another-long-random-string
# Keys /takedown's IP match (design 137). Optional: without it the
# abuse limits match requesters by email alone.
TAKEDOWN_SECRET=generate-a-third-long-random-string
# Required locally: wrangler.jsonc sets the production origin
# (https://dialed.run). Without this override Better Auth refuses every
# sign-in and sign-up from localhost (403 INVALID_ORIGIN), and the https
# posture turns its rate limiter on. Match the port the dev server runs on.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Required to sign up locally (125, OPS-5): wrangler.jsonc sets the site key
# to "", and with no key the widget renders nothing and the server refuses
# every sign-up. These are Cloudflare's published always-pass test keys —
# public, the same pair CI writes — not secrets. Missing either one makes
# `npm run demo` time out in `turnstileAnswered` with nothing in the
# console, which looks like a blocked network and is not one.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=1x00000000000000000000AA
# "Import from Garmin" (plan 157): your own Garmin Connect Personal API key
# and your own dialed.run user id (the key is for its holder's data only).
# Both or neither; without them the import is not drawn.
# GARMIN_API_KEY=
# GARMIN_OWNER_USER_ID=
# Optional locally; set in prod:
# SENTRY_DSN=
# Google OAuth (both or neither — the Google button 500s without them):
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Enrichment's LLM rung (107). One key covers every external candidate —
# that is why OpenRouter is the route rather than a vendor SDK. Needed to
# run the model eval, not to run the app: a missing key degrades the
# ladder to its deterministic rungs (law 5), it does not fail a save.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Photo screening (106). The classifier that decides whether a photo is
# safe for strangers to see. Without it every uploaded photo stays
# `pending`: its owner sees it, nobody else does, and the hourly
# `screening-retry` sweep screens the backlog once the key exists. So a
# missing key degrades visibility, it never fails an upload (law 5).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Who can reach the review queue at /safety/review (106) and, later, The
# Desk. A comma-separated list of user ids; unset or empty means NOBODY is
# an admin, which fails closed. There is no `vars` block in
# wrangler.jsonc, so this file is the only place it can be set locally —
# which is also why the admin surfaces have no demo video yet (R-72).
# ADMIN_USER_IDS=
